# UI rules

## The aesthetic in one sentence

Byzantine imperial court — dark, refined, parchment + deep burgundy +
aged gold. Not generic medieval fantasy.

## Color tokens

All colors live as CSS variables in `app/globals.css`:

- `--color-ink` — near-black background tone
- `--color-parchment` / `parchment-dark` / `parchment-deep` — body text
  family, light-on-dark
- `--color-imperial` / `imperial-deep` / `imperial-shadow` — burgundies
- `--color-gold` / `gold-dim` / `gold-bright` — accents and headings
- `--color-verdigris` — accent green (gems, secondary actions)
- `--color-blood` — error, danger
- `--color-bone`, `--color-ash` — neutral surfaces

Tailwind aliases these as `bg-imperial`, `text-gold`, etc. Use the
Tailwind aliases from components; reach into `rgb(var(--color-*))` from
inside SVG attributes or inline styles where Tailwind can't reach.

The variables themselves store space-separated RGB triples without an
alpha channel (e.g. `--color-gold: 201 164 76;`). Tailwind's opacity
modifiers (`bg-gold/20`, `text-parchment/80`) compose them via
`rgb(var(--color-X) / <alpha-value>)`.

## Typography

- Display headings (`h1`–`h4`, panel headings, buttons): **Cinzel**, via
  the `font-display` Tailwind family. Letter-spaced, often uppercase.
- Body text: **Lora**, via `font-body` (the default `body` style).
- Decorative serif (italics, blurbs): **Cormorant Garamond**, via
  `font-serif`.
- Never introduce sans-serif. Never use system-ui defaults.

## Reusable component classes

Defined in `app/globals.css` under `@layer components`:

- `.panel` — bordered, gold-trimmed surface
- `.panel-heading` — uppercase tracking-imperial heading bar
- `.panel-body` — padded inner area
- `.btn-imperial` — primary action button
- `.btn-ghost` — secondary action button
- `.input-imperial` — form input
- `.label-imperial` — form label
- `.divider-laurel` — gold gradient divider line

Prefer composing these over inventing new ones. If you need a new
primitive, add it to `globals.css` so it's available globally.

## Numbers

Always use `tabular-nums` for currency, AP, stats. Localised digits
(`Number.toLocaleString("en-US")` or `Intl.NumberFormat`) for thousands
separators in coin amounts.

## Voice

Copy is restrained and slightly archaic.

- "Forge a new identity in the empire."
- "The dice are cast at every midnight."
- "Your saddlebag is empty. Work, trade, or fight to fill it."

Avoid: "Welcome adventurer!", "Let's go!", "Awesome!", emojis.
